					"font-size": {
						"type": "float",
						"value": 19
					},
					"text": {
						"type": "string",
						"value": "QUANTIZE\n\nThe Quantize node quantizes the incoming value or texture.\nThis allows you to quantize the signal into descrete steps.\n\nQuantization can be useful when you need to \"round\"  values into steps. Essentially reducing the resolution of a signal and preventing certain values to appear.\n\nWhen you set the step size to 3.0, the resulting values are 0, 3, 6, 9 etc"
					}
				},
				"bounds": {
					"height": 226.2762298583984375,
					"width": 538.36639404296875,
					"x": 206.935302734375,
					"y": 150.7178802490234375
				},
				"class": {
					"id": "77697265-3C1D-467D-A722-0FC566538374",
					"version": 1
