						"value": 19
					},
					"text": {
						"type": "string",
						"value": "EXAMPLE 2: QUANTIZING A TEXTURE\n\nIn this example we are quantizing the channels of the test card.\nThe same concept applies here, we are taking the color data and quantizing it into discrete steps.\n\nFor example: by quantizing the blue channel to steps of 0.5 we are forcing the color to be either 0, 0.5 or 1. In other words: black, 50% grey or white.\n\nIt is possible to quantize either texture2Drgba or texture2Dchannel.\nThe advantage of quantizing the channels is that you can apply different levels of quantization to each channel."
					}
				},
